_data": [], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn8le15ob09re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "text": "", "id": 0, "image": "engenn8le15ob09re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "100", "text": "Dear Dr. Brook,\n<br/><br/>\nI was recently diagnosed with prostate cancer. Because I am about 65 pounds overweight, I was told that the surgery could not be performed unless I embarked on a weight loss program immediately. I sought a second opinion. Now, I have been offered an opening for the removal of my\ncancerous prostate if I opt for a robotic surgical system. <br/>\nAlthough the operation cannot be considered anything but essential, the idea of being cut open and operated on by a robot frightens me. How safely can the procedure be done with a robot at the helm?  What are my chances of recovery if I go ahead with it?<br/><br/>\nPetrified with Prostate Cancer\n<br/><br/>\n...", "id": 1, "image": "engenn8le15ob09re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "47000", "text": "Dear Petrified, <br/><br/>\nIf I understand correctly, you are more worried about a robotic surgeon than by the surgery itself. Let me reassure you: the use of a robotic system in prostate surgery is a miraculous in medical science. The prostate is located deep within the pelvis, so It can be reached only with difficulty in overweight patients.", "id": 2, "image": "engenn8le15ob09re2img03.jpg"}, {"time": "73000", "text": "If they have the procedure, they may develop serious complications following it. <br/>\nIf you choose the robotic system it will increase the chance of a successful operation while decreasing the chance of complications. Your recovery rate could even be higher than a patient who is not overweight. <br/><br/>\nGood luck, <br/><br/>Doctor Brook", "id": 3, "image": "engenn8le15ob09re2img03.jpg"}], "coverimg": "engenn8le15ob09re2img01.jpg"}}], "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "id": 1}, {"contents": [{"type": "p", "value": "Dear Dr. Harrison,<br/><br/>\nMy name is Anna . When I was 45 years old I was diagnosed with breast cancer. I had a breast conserving surgery. Now I am 47 years old and I am supposed to undergo radiation therapy. I suppose I'll have to do it because  the cancer is spreading. I wonder  if you may give me advice regarding the right procedure. Is it really necessary to undergo radiation therapy or should I seek a second option? I have heard great things about the robotic surgical system. Is this type of procedure  common in my case?\n"}], "template_override": 1, "type": "text", "title": "", "_data": [], "id": 2}]}]}